WEBVTT

00:00:13.382 --> 00:00:15.584
Cambridge Discovery Readers.

00:00:15.644 --> 00:00:17.304
Starter Level.

00:00:17.364 --> 00:00:20.316
Gone by Margaret Johnson.

00:00:20.376 --> 00:00:23.448
Published by Cambridge University Press.

00:00:23.508 --> 00:00:35.835
This recording is copyright.

00:00:35.895 --> 00:00:55.628
Chapter 1 Birthday Boy I'm sorry I'm working on your birthday, Tom.

00:00:55.688 --> 00:00:59.120
Tom's mother is leaving the house.

00:00:59.180 --> 00:01:01.382
She isn't looking at Tom.

00:01:01.442 --> 00:01:04.074
She's thinking about work.

00:01:04.134 --> 00:01:06.416
Have a nice day, love.

00:01:06.476 --> 00:01:09.840
See you tonight, she says.

00:01:09.900 --> 00:01:13.342
Goodbye, Mom, Tom says.

00:01:13.402 --> 00:01:15.334
He feels sad.

00:01:15.394 --> 00:01:18.316
He doesn't want her to go.

00:01:18.376 --> 00:01:23.487
Tom's sister, Annie, comes down from her room.

00:01:23.547 --> 00:01:27.428
Happy birthday, little brother, she says.

00:01:27.488 --> 00:01:29.609
12 today.

00:01:29.669 --> 00:01:31.820
Tom smiles.

00:01:31.880 --> 00:01:34.511
He likes being 12.

00:01:34.570 --> 00:01:38.462
Can I give you your birthday present this afternoon?

00:01:38.522 --> 00:01:39.922
Annie asks.

00:01:39.982 --> 00:01:43.607
I'm going shopping this morning with my friends.

00:01:43.666 --> 00:01:46.442
She goes to the door.

00:01:46.502 --> 00:01:49.072
I want to go shopping.

00:01:49.132 --> 00:01:53.364
Tom starts to say, but Annie doesn't hear.

00:01:53.424 --> 00:01:56.606
Enjoy your birthday, she says.

00:01:56.666 --> 00:01:59.498
Then she leaves too.

00:01:59.558 --> 00:02:04.601
Now Tom's father is the only person at home.

00:02:04.660 --> 00:02:07.562
Tom finds him at his desk.

00:02:07.622 --> 00:02:10.666
He's working on his computer.

00:02:10.726 --> 00:02:17.221
Tom's father works at home, and he works all the time.

00:02:17.280 --> 00:02:23.833
Tom walks into his father's office, and his father turns and looks at him.

00:02:23.893 --> 00:02:26.954
Hello, Tom, he says.

00:02:27.014 --> 00:02:29.826
What are you going to do with your birthday money?

00:02:29.846 --> 00:02:34.268
I don't know, Dad, Tom says.

00:02:34.328 --> 00:02:36.698
Can we go shopping?

00:02:36.758 --> 00:02:41.166
Tom's father is looking at his computer again.

00:02:41.226 --> 00:02:44.203
Not to dear Tom, he says.

00:02:44.263 --> 00:02:46.314
I must finish this work.

00:02:46.374 --> 00:02:48.075
Where's Annie?

00:02:48.135 --> 00:02:52.417
She's shopping with her friends, Tom says.

00:02:52.477 --> 00:02:55.698
He knows his father isn't listening.

00:02:55.758 --> 00:02:59.100
He's reading an email on his computer.

00:02:59.160 --> 00:03:02.022
That's nice, he says.

00:03:02.081 --> 00:03:04.433
But he doesn't look at Tom.

00:03:04.493 --> 00:03:06.744
Have a good time.

00:03:06.804 --> 00:03:11.999
Okay, says Tom, and he leaves the room.

00:03:12.059 --> 00:03:15.844
Tom phones his friend, Neil.

00:03:15.903 --> 00:03:18.606
Neil's mother answers.

00:03:18.665 --> 00:03:20.947
Can I speak to Neil?

00:03:21.007 --> 00:03:22.608
Tom asks.

00:03:22.668 --> 00:03:25.811
I'm sorry, Neil's mother says.

00:03:25.870 --> 00:03:29.203
He's playing football in Winston Park.

00:03:29.263 --> 00:03:31.004
Is that Tom?

00:03:31.064 --> 00:03:34.016
Yes, says Tom.

00:03:34.076 --> 00:03:39.150
Neil tells me it's your birthday today, Neil's mother says.

00:03:39.210 --> 00:03:41.381
Happy birthday.

00:03:41.441 --> 00:03:42.834
Thank you.

00:03:42.894 --> 00:03:43.725
says Tom.

00:03:43.745 --> 00:03:48.946
"'I must go, but have a good day,' says Neil's mother.

00:03:48.966 --> 00:03:53.968
"'Thank you,' Tom says again, and he puts the phone down.

00:03:53.988 --> 00:03:59.049
"'No one has any time for me today,' he thinks.

00:03:59.069 --> 00:04:05.260
"'It's my birthday, and no one has any time for me."

00:04:05.320 --> 00:04:16.130
Chapter 2 The Camera Tom leaves the house and walks to Winston Park.

00:04:16.190 --> 00:04:20.902
He doesn't like football, but he wants to be with people.

00:04:20.962 --> 00:04:23.203
It's a hot day.

00:04:23.263 --> 00:04:28.916
In Winston Park, there are lots of mothers and fathers with their children.

00:04:28.976 --> 00:04:32.468
Boys and girls are running and laughing.

00:04:32.528 --> 00:04:34.910
Everyone looks happy.

00:04:34.970 --> 00:04:38.491
Tom sees Neil and some more boys.

00:04:38.551 --> 00:04:40.740
They're playing football.

00:04:40.799 --> 00:04:43.018
Tom goes over.

00:04:43.078 --> 00:04:44.688
Neil sees him.

00:04:44.748 --> 00:04:46.458
He smiles.

00:04:46.518 --> 00:04:48.229
Hello, Tom.

00:04:48.289 --> 00:04:49.560
He calls.

00:04:49.619 --> 00:04:51.840
Happy birthday.

00:04:51.900 --> 00:04:53.651
Thank you.

00:04:53.711 --> 00:04:54.941
Tom calls.

00:04:55.001 --> 00:04:58.112
But Neil is running to get the ball.

00:04:58.172 --> 00:05:01.713
Tom watches the game for 10 minutes.

00:05:01.773 --> 00:05:04.504
But Neil doesn't speak to him again.

00:05:04.564 --> 00:05:09.090
Neil's good at football and he's enjoying the game.

00:05:09.150 --> 00:05:13.566
Tom starts walking across Winston Park.

00:05:13.626 --> 00:05:18.698
He sits down on a seat and takes a drink from his bag.

00:05:18.758 --> 00:05:21.459
He puts his bag down.

00:05:21.519 --> 00:05:24.850
There is another bag under the seat.

00:05:24.910 --> 00:05:26.451
What's this?

00:05:26.510 --> 00:05:28.061
Thinks Tom.

00:05:28.121 --> 00:05:30.492
The bag is black.

00:05:30.552 --> 00:05:32.833
Tom opens it.

00:05:32.892 --> 00:05:35.394
He's looking for a name.

00:05:35.453 --> 00:05:38.734
There is only one thing in the bag.

00:05:38.794 --> 00:05:40.490
A camera.

00:05:40.550 --> 00:05:42.966
Tom takes it out.

00:05:43.026 --> 00:05:46.116
Then he looks in the bag again.

00:05:46.176 --> 00:05:48.127
But there is nothing in it.

00:05:48.187 --> 00:05:50.168
No name.

00:05:50.228 --> 00:05:53.299
Tom looks at the camera.

00:05:53.359 --> 00:05:55.450
There are four buttons.

00:05:55.510 --> 00:06:00.531
Photo, delete, on and off.

00:06:00.591 --> 00:06:05.343
Tom puts his finger on the on button and presses it.

00:06:05.402 --> 00:06:07.953
The camera makes a noise.

00:06:08.013 --> 00:06:10.984
The black bag is on the seat.

00:06:11.044 --> 00:06:14.086
Tom can see it in the camera.

00:06:14.146 --> 00:06:17.779
Tom puts his finger on the photo button.

00:06:17.839 --> 00:06:19.360
He presses it.

00:06:19.420 --> 00:06:22.532
The camera makes another noise.

00:06:22.592 --> 00:06:25.654
Tom looks at the photo of the bag.

00:06:25.714 --> 00:06:32.890
It's okay, but he doesn't want a photo of a bag, so he presses the delete button.

00:06:32.950 --> 00:06:35.522
The photo goes away.

00:06:35.582 --> 00:06:38.044
This camera is okay.

00:06:38.104 --> 00:06:39.456
Tom thinks.

00:06:39.516 --> 00:06:41.746
But it isn't my camera.

00:06:41.806 --> 00:06:44.218
I must take it to the police.

00:06:44.278 --> 00:06:47.950
I can buy a camera with my birthday money.

00:06:48.010 --> 00:06:52.812
Tom puts out his hand to take the camera bag from the seat.

00:06:52.872 --> 00:06:55.683
But the bag isn't there.

00:06:55.743 --> 00:06:58.234
He looks under the seat.

00:06:58.294 --> 00:06:59.865
No bag.

00:06:59.925 --> 00:07:02.306
He looks behind the seat.

00:07:02.366 --> 00:07:04.087
No bag.

00:07:04.147 --> 00:07:06.860
Tom doesn't understand.

00:07:06.920 --> 00:07:09.184
Where is the bag?

00:07:09.244 --> 00:07:10.984
He thinks.

00:07:11.044 --> 00:07:14.465
A squirrel runs in front of the seat.

00:07:14.525 --> 00:07:16.876
Tom wants a photo of it.

00:07:16.936 --> 00:07:19.267
The squirrel stops.

00:07:19.327 --> 00:07:23.018
It's looking for food, Tom thinks.

00:07:23.078 --> 00:07:26.809
He smiles and presses the photo button.

00:07:26.869 --> 00:07:30.950
But when he looks at the photo, it isn't good.

00:07:31.010 --> 00:07:35.550
Squirrels are too fast for photos, Tom thinks.

00:07:35.610 --> 00:07:38.140
He presses the delete button.

00:07:38.200 --> 00:07:41.392
The photo of the squirrel goes away.

00:07:41.452 --> 00:07:46.376
When Tom looks for the squirrel, he can't see it.

00:07:46.436 --> 00:07:50.080
Squirrels run fast, Tom thinks.

00:07:50.140 --> 00:07:52.031
But not that fast.

00:07:52.091 --> 00:07:53.872
Where is it?

00:07:53.932 --> 00:07:56.574
Tom looks at the camera.

00:07:56.634 --> 00:07:58.536
He doesn't understand.

00:07:58.596 --> 00:08:00.498
Something is wrong.

00:08:00.558 --> 00:08:03.554
He wants to try the camera again.

00:08:03.614 --> 00:08:06.810
There are some flowers next to his seat.

00:08:06.870 --> 00:08:09.432
Tom looks at the camera again.

00:08:09.492 --> 00:08:11.614
He can see the flowers.

00:08:11.674 --> 00:08:17.120
He presses the photo button and takes a photo of the flowers.

00:08:17.180 --> 00:08:22.705
Then he presses the delete button to make the photo go away.

00:08:22.765 --> 00:08:26.638
Tom takes the camera away from his face.

00:08:26.698 --> 00:08:28.951
He looks for the flowers.

00:08:29.010 --> 00:08:31.290
They aren't there.

00:08:31.350 --> 00:08:38.090
The flowers are gone, he thinks.

00:08:38.150 --> 00:08:40.851
Chapter 3.

00:08:40.911 --> 00:08:43.932
Where's the ball?

00:08:43.992 --> 00:08:47.684
Tom puts the camera down.

00:08:47.744 --> 00:08:50.516
He doesn't want it in his hands now.

00:08:50.576 --> 00:08:52.456
He feels afraid.

00:08:52.516 --> 00:08:58.041
He thinks about the camera bag, the squirrel and the flowers.

00:08:58.102 --> 00:09:04.708
When I take photos of things with this camera, they go away, he thinks.

00:09:04.768 --> 00:09:08.260
I don't know how, but they do.

00:09:08.320 --> 00:09:13.482
Across Winston Park, he can see the boys playing football.

00:09:13.542 --> 00:09:17.504
I must tell Neil about this, he thinks.

00:09:17.564 --> 00:09:23.178
He puts the camera in his bag and starts running across the park.

00:09:23.238 --> 00:09:26.766
But after a minute, he stops running.

00:09:26.826 --> 00:09:31.762
He thinks about the camera bag, the squirrel and the flowers.

00:09:31.822 --> 00:09:34.452
He's near the boys now.

00:09:34.512 --> 00:09:37.973
It's my birthday, he thinks.

00:09:38.033 --> 00:09:41.403
I want Neil to come to the shops with me.

00:09:41.463 --> 00:09:43.384
We can get a pizza.

00:09:43.444 --> 00:09:47.554
I can buy something with my birthday money.

00:09:47.614 --> 00:09:51.895
A boy in a blue t-shirt has the ball now.

00:09:51.955 --> 00:09:53.896
He's running fast.

00:09:53.956 --> 00:09:56.879
Then everyone shouts.

00:09:56.939 --> 00:09:58.672
No!

00:09:58.732 --> 00:10:03.254
Lots of the boys run to the boy in the blue t-shirt.

00:10:03.314 --> 00:10:05.724
They are all very happy.

00:10:05.784 --> 00:10:11.036
Tom quickly takes the camera from the bag and looks into it.

00:10:11.096 --> 00:10:13.416
He can see the ball.

00:10:13.476 --> 00:10:19.248
He presses the photo button and then the delete button.

00:10:19.308 --> 00:10:22.890
The boys want to start playing again.

00:10:22.950 --> 00:10:26.871
Hey, shouts the boy in the blue t-shirt.

00:10:26.931 --> 00:10:29.092
Where's the ball?

00:10:29.152 --> 00:10:31.973
No one can understand.

00:10:32.033 --> 00:10:36.104
They look on the grass and behind trees.

00:10:36.164 --> 00:10:38.665
Can you see the ball, Tom?

00:10:38.725 --> 00:10:40.226
Neil asks.

00:10:40.286 --> 00:10:43.807
No, sorry, Tom says.

00:10:43.867 --> 00:10:46.608
I don't know where the ball is.

00:10:46.668 --> 00:10:49.579
I don't think you can play now.

00:10:49.639 --> 00:10:52.010
Do you want to get a pizza with me?

00:10:52.030 --> 00:10:56.414
I can buy something to eat with my birthday money."

00:10:56.474 --> 00:10:59.315
But Neil doesn't hear Tom.

00:10:59.376 --> 00:11:02.828
He's listening to the boy in the blue t-shirt.

00:11:02.888 --> 00:11:05.480
It's okay, he says.

00:11:05.540 --> 00:11:08.222
I've got another ball in my bag.

00:11:08.282 --> 00:11:10.544
Good, says Neil.

00:11:10.604 --> 00:11:13.206
But where is our other ball?

00:11:13.266 --> 00:11:16.299
I don't know, says the boy.

00:11:16.359 --> 00:11:19.352
He gets the new ball from his bag.

00:11:19.411 --> 00:11:21.852
They start to play again.

00:11:21.912 --> 00:11:28.496
Tom thinks about taking a new photo, a photo of the new ball.

00:11:28.556 --> 00:11:36.230
But the boys run away across the grass, and Tom turns and starts to walk home.

00:11:36.291 --> 00:11:47.604
Chapter 4 The Computer When Tom gets home, his father is making a coffee.

00:11:47.664 --> 00:11:50.845
Tom, is that you?

00:11:50.905 --> 00:11:52.366
He calls.

00:11:52.426 --> 00:11:55.467
Yes, Tom answers.

00:11:55.527 --> 00:11:57.417
Do you want a coffee?

00:11:57.477 --> 00:11:59.308
His father asks.

00:11:59.368 --> 00:12:00.958
No, thank you.

00:12:01.018 --> 00:12:02.419
Answers, Tom.

00:12:02.479 --> 00:12:05.690
I'm just getting something from my room.

00:12:05.750 --> 00:12:09.691
Tom quickly runs up to his father's office.

00:12:09.751 --> 00:12:12.346
It's the room with the computer.

00:12:12.406 --> 00:12:15.301
He takes the camera from his bag.

00:12:15.361 --> 00:12:17.964
He can see the computer in it.

00:12:18.024 --> 00:12:22.648
He quickly presses photo, then delete.

00:12:22.708 --> 00:12:24.930
He looks at the table.

00:12:24.990 --> 00:12:26.811
No computer.

00:12:26.871 --> 00:12:29.714
Good, he thinks.

00:12:29.774 --> 00:12:33.827
Tom's father comes into the room with his coffee.

00:12:33.887 --> 00:12:35.959
He smiles at Tom.

00:12:36.018 --> 00:12:38.421
Okay, he asks.

00:12:38.481 --> 00:12:41.098
Then he stops smiling.

00:12:41.158 --> 00:12:43.174
Where's my computer?"

00:12:43.234 --> 00:12:44.935
he asks.

00:12:44.995 --> 00:12:48.496
I don't know, says Tom.

00:12:48.556 --> 00:12:52.597
I don't understand, Tom's father says.

00:12:52.657 --> 00:12:54.247
Where is it?

00:12:54.307 --> 00:12:56.758
He looks behind Tom.

00:12:56.818 --> 00:12:59.498
He looks under the table.

00:12:59.558 --> 00:13:02.599
He looks all over the room.

00:13:02.659 --> 00:13:05.920
Then he looks at Tom.

00:13:05.980 --> 00:13:10.364
Tom, he says, where's my computer?

00:13:10.424 --> 00:13:14.008
I don't know, answers Tom.

00:13:14.068 --> 00:13:18.672
Computers don't just go, Tom's father says.

00:13:18.732 --> 00:13:22.256
Yes they do, thinks Tom.

00:13:22.316 --> 00:13:25.148
Then he looks at his father.

00:13:25.208 --> 00:13:27.580
Can we go to the shops dad?

00:13:27.640 --> 00:13:28.902
He asks.

00:13:28.962 --> 00:13:32.184
Nor Tom, his father says.

00:13:32.244 --> 00:13:34.696
I must find my computer.

00:13:34.757 --> 00:13:37.161
I'm going to phone the police.

00:13:37.220 --> 00:13:43.214
After the police come, Tom says, can we go to the shops then?

00:13:43.274 --> 00:13:48.405
But Tom's father can't stop thinking about his computer.

00:13:48.465 --> 00:13:53.626
Please Tom, he says, he looks tired.

00:13:53.686 --> 00:13:58.407
I know it's your birthday, but all my work is on that computer.

00:13:58.467 --> 00:14:00.367
It's very important.

00:14:00.427 --> 00:14:03.058
I don't know what to do.

00:14:03.118 --> 00:14:05.925
Tom looks at his father.

00:14:05.984 --> 00:14:09.202
I'm sorry, Dad," he says.

00:14:09.262 --> 00:14:12.304
His father smiles a little.

00:14:12.364 --> 00:14:15.866
It's okay, son, he says.

00:14:15.926 --> 00:14:18.838
Go and enjoy your birthday.

00:14:18.898 --> 00:14:21.500
Tom leaves the room.

00:14:21.560 --> 00:14:25.232
I can't enjoy my birthday, he thinks.

00:14:25.292 --> 00:14:28.284
No one has any time for me.

00:14:28.344 --> 00:14:32.556
Tom goes to his room and sits on his bed.

00:14:32.616 --> 00:14:35.695
Then he thinks about his mother.

00:14:35.755 --> 00:14:39.262
and he knows what he wants to do.

00:14:39.322 --> 00:14:42.093
CHAPTER V.

00:14:42.153 --> 00:14:53.355
TRYING TO HELP Tom leaves the house and walks to his mother's cafe, Kathy's coffee shop.

00:14:53.415 --> 00:14:57.116
The cafe sells food all day.

00:14:57.176 --> 00:15:00.396
Lots of people go there on Saturdays.

00:15:00.456 --> 00:15:03.717
Tom can see his mother in the cafe.

00:15:03.777 --> 00:15:05.536
She looks hot.

00:15:05.596 --> 00:15:11.468
There are people at all the tables, and they're all waiting for their food.

00:15:11.528 --> 00:15:14.980
Mum's tired, Tom thinks.

00:15:15.041 --> 00:15:17.232
She works a lot.

00:15:17.292 --> 00:15:19.844
He goes into the cafe.

00:15:19.904 --> 00:15:22.065
His mother sees him.

00:15:22.126 --> 00:15:25.127
Hello, Tom, she says.

00:15:25.188 --> 00:15:28.200
Why are you here on your birthday?

00:15:28.260 --> 00:15:31.922
I'm here to help you, he says.

00:15:31.982 --> 00:15:34.586
His mother smiles.

00:15:34.646 --> 00:15:38.400
Oh, thank you, Tom," she says.

00:15:38.460 --> 00:15:43.772
People want plates and cups for their food and drinks, she says.

00:15:43.832 --> 00:15:45.973
They're all dirty.

00:15:46.033 --> 00:15:51.135
She takes Tom to the dirty plates and cups in the kitchen.

00:15:51.195 --> 00:15:53.436
Can you wash them for me?

00:15:53.496 --> 00:15:54.897
She asks.

00:15:54.956 --> 00:15:56.907
Tom smiles.

00:15:56.967 --> 00:15:59.498
Of course, he says.

00:15:59.558 --> 00:16:02.464
Tom's mother smiles again.

00:16:02.524 --> 00:16:05.960
You're a good boy, she says.

00:16:06.020 --> 00:16:08.521
Then she leaves the kitchen.

00:16:08.581 --> 00:16:12.832
Tom quickly takes the camera from his bag.

00:16:12.892 --> 00:16:16.993
I can have an afternoon with Mum, he thinks.

00:16:17.053 --> 00:16:21.134
We can go to a restaurant or watch a film.

00:16:21.194 --> 00:16:25.704
He can see the dirty cups and plates in the camera.

00:16:25.764 --> 00:16:29.415
He presses photo, then delete.

00:16:29.475 --> 00:16:33.837
Then he takes the camera away and looks.

00:16:33.897 --> 00:16:36.460
Gone, he thinks.

00:16:36.520 --> 00:16:37.930
They're gone.

00:16:37.990 --> 00:16:40.032
And he smiles.

00:16:40.092 --> 00:16:43.234
His mother comes back into the kitchen.

00:16:43.294 --> 00:16:45.626
She looks all over the room.

00:16:45.686 --> 00:16:48.298
Tom, she says.

00:16:48.358 --> 00:16:50.810
Where are the cups and plates?

00:16:50.870 --> 00:16:53.752
Tom thinks for a few seconds.

00:16:53.812 --> 00:16:56.805
It's the camera, he tells her.

00:16:56.864 --> 00:17:00.837
When I take a photo, things go away.

00:17:00.897 --> 00:17:03.211
His mother looks at him.

00:17:03.271 --> 00:17:06.044
She looks very tired now.

00:17:06.104 --> 00:17:07.574
What?

00:17:07.634 --> 00:17:09.114
She asks.

00:17:09.174 --> 00:17:11.514
I don't understand.

00:17:11.574 --> 00:17:16.695
The camera, Tom starts, but his mother speaks.

00:17:16.755 --> 00:17:24.737
Tom, she says, there aren't any plates or cups, and there are lots of people in the cafe.

00:17:24.797 --> 00:17:27.047
What am I going to do?

00:17:27.107 --> 00:17:29.338
Close the cafe, ma'am.

00:17:29.398 --> 00:17:32.667
Tom says, we can go out.

00:17:32.727 --> 00:17:35.447
His mother is angry now.

00:17:35.507 --> 00:17:39.698
I can't close the cafe, Tom, she says.

00:17:39.759 --> 00:17:41.760
This is my job.

00:17:41.820 --> 00:17:46.522
Now please, tell me where the cups and plates are.

00:17:46.582 --> 00:17:48.552
I don't know, mum.

00:17:48.612 --> 00:17:52.734
Tom starts saying, it's the camera.

00:17:52.794 --> 00:17:54.815
The door opens.

00:17:54.875 --> 00:17:56.986
Tom's sister comes in.

00:17:57.046 --> 00:17:59.146
Hello, she says.

00:17:59.206 --> 00:18:00.611
What's wrong?

00:18:00.671 --> 00:18:05.328
Tom's mother starts telling Annie about the plates and cups.

00:18:05.388 --> 00:18:07.370
But Annie isn't listening.

00:18:07.430 --> 00:18:09.922
She sees Tom's camera.

00:18:09.981 --> 00:18:11.533
What's this?

00:18:11.593 --> 00:18:15.076
She says, and takes it from her brother.

00:18:15.136 --> 00:18:16.747
Is it new?

00:18:16.807 --> 00:18:19.710
Give it to me, Tom says.

00:18:19.770 --> 00:18:21.650
Annie doesn't listen.

00:18:21.710 --> 00:18:24.443
She puts the camera to her eye.

00:18:24.503 --> 00:18:26.324
She looks at Tom.

00:18:26.384 --> 00:18:29.140
Smile, she says.

00:18:29.200 --> 00:18:31.916
No, Tom shouts.

00:18:31.976 --> 00:18:34.760
Annie presses the photo button.

00:18:34.820 --> 00:18:37.124
Give the camera to me, Annie.

00:18:37.184 --> 00:18:38.576
Tom shouts.

00:18:38.636 --> 00:18:40.989
Annie looks at the photo.

00:18:41.049 --> 00:18:45.235
This isn't a good photo of you, Tom, Annie says.

00:18:45.295 --> 00:18:48.259
No, don't press any buttons.

00:18:48.319 --> 00:18:51.443
Shouts, Tom, but it's too late.

00:18:51.504 --> 00:18:54.097
Annie presses, delete.

